.TH RUSTRANSLATOR 1 "2026-10-10" "rustranslator 0.1.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustranslator \- markdown translation with a local translator and a cloud reviewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustranslator
.I config show
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR path ]
.br
.B rustranslator
.B mcp
.RB [ \-\-transport
.IR stdio | http ]
.RB [ \-\-address
.IR IP:PORT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustranslator
translates markdown documentation in short blocks: a local model writes the translation and a
cloud model reviews it, so that only the flagged residue needs to be read by a person.
.PP
The program also exposes itself as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, for agents that speak
that protocol. It offers seven tools: echo, submit, status, result, cancel, translate and
review. A whole document takes three calls -- submit, then status, then result -- because submit
returns at once and the work runs in the background; cancel is read between blocks, and every
block already done stays in the registry.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config show
Prints the configuration in force, the path of the file it came from, and the masked API key.
It exists so you can check what the program actually read, instead of assuming.
.TP
.B mcp
Starts the MCP server. With
.B \-\-transport stdio
(the default) the client itself spawns the process and holds the pipes. With
.B \-\-transport http
the server answers on
.BR http://ADDRESS/mcp ,
which is the mode systemd can keep alive.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustranslator/config.json
User configuration. This is where the token lives; mode 0600 is recommended.
.TP
.I /etc/rustranslator/config.json
System default, holding no secret at all.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rustranslator/
Working directory: the block-by-block registry, the task state and the report of flagged blocks.
.SH CONFIGURATION SEARCH ORDER
the value of
.BR \-\-config ,
then
.BR $RUSTRANSLATOR_CONFIG ,
then
.I ~/.config/rustranslator/config.json
and finally
.IR /etc/rustranslator/config.json .
The first one that exists wins.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.ft CR
rustranslator config show
rustranslator mcp --transport http --address 127.0.0.1:9720
.ft
.fi
